  "title": "Aqiqah (Ritual Sacrifice for the Newborn)",
  "data": "It is reported that the following should be said when slaughtering the animal offered as aqiqah in the name of the newborn:\nبِسْمِ اللّٰهِ وَبِاللّٰهِ اَللّٰهُمَّ عَقِيْقَةٌ عَنْ فُلَانٍ\nBISMILLAAHI WA BILLAAHI ALLAAHUMMA A'QEEQATUN A'N FULAAN\nIn the Name of Allah and by Allah. O Allah, (this is) an aqiqah for so-and-so:\nلَحْمُهَا بِلَحْمِهٖ وَدَمُهَا بِدَمِهٖ وَعَظْمُهَا بِعَظْمِهٖ اَللّٰهُمَّ اجْعَلْهَا وِقَاۤءً لِاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ عَلَيْهِ وَاٰلِهِ السَّلَامُ\nLAHMUHAA BILAHMIHEE WA DAMUHAA BIDAMIHEE WA A'ZMUHAA BI-A'ZMIHEE ALLAAHUMMAJ A'LHAA WIQAA'AN LI-AALI MUHAMMADIN A'LAYHI WA AALIHIS SALAAM\nits flesh for his flesh, its blood for his blood, and its bones for his bones. O Allah, make it a protection for the family of Muhammad, peace be upon him and his Household.\nIn place of “so-and-so”, mention the newborn's name.\nAccording to another tradition, the following may be said when slaughtering an animal as an offering to Almighty Allah for the newborn:\nيَا قَوْمِ اِنِّىْ بَرِىْۤءٌ مِمَّا تُشْرِكُوْنَ اِنِّىْ وَجَّهْتُ وَجْهِىَ لِلَّذِىْ فَطَرَ السَّمٰوَاتِ وَالْاَرْضَ حَنِيْفًا مُّسْلِمًا وَمَا اَنَا مِنَ الْمُشْرِكِيْنَ\nYAA QAWMI INNEE BAREE'UN MIMMAA TUSHRIKOONA INNEE WAJJAHTU WAJHIYA LILLADHEE FATARAS SAMAAWAATI WAL ARDA HANEEFAM MUSLIMAN WA MAA ANAA MINAL MUSHRIKEEN\nO my people! surely I am clear of what you set up (with Allah). Surely I have turned my face, being upright, wholly to Him Who originated the heavens and the earth, as a Muslim, and I am not of the polytheists. (6:78-79)\nاِنَّ صَلَاتِىْ وَنُسُكِىْ وَمَحْيَاىَ وَمَمَاتِىْ لِلّٰهِ رَبِّ الْعَالَمِيْنَ لَا شَرِيْكَ لَهٗ وَبِذٰلِكَ اُمِرْتُ وَاَنَا مِنَ الْمُسْلِمِيْنَ\nINNA SALAATEE WA NUSUKEE WA MAHYAAYA WA MAMAATEE LILLAAHI RABBIL A'ALAMEENA LAA SHAREEKA LAHOO WA BIDHAALIKA UMIRTU WA ANAA MINAL MUSLIMEEN\nSurely my prayer, my sacrifice, my life and my death are (all) for Allah, the Lord of the worlds; no associate has He; and this am I commanded, and I am of those who submit. (6:162-163)\nاَللّٰهُمَّ مِنْكَ وَلَكَ بِسْمِ اللّٰهِ وَبِاللّٰهِ وَاللّٰهُ اَكْبَرُ اَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَّاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ وَّتَقَبَّلْ مِنْ فُلَانِ بْنِ فُلَانٍ\nALLAAHUMMA MINKA WA LAKA BISMILLAAHI WA BILLAAHI WALLAAHU AKBARU ALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMADIN WA TAQABBAL MIN FULAANIBNI FULAAN\nO Allah, (it is) from You and for You. In the Name of Allah and by Allah, and Allah is the Greatest. O Allah, bless Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad, and accept (it) from so-and-so, the son of so-and-so.\nIn place of “so-and-so, the son of so-and-so”, mention the newborn's name and his father's name. One may then slaughter the animal."
}
